import sys,os,re
from pathlib import Path
from lesson_writer import author,CPP
relative='src/org/minima/system/commands/network/ping.md'
author(relative,'Sends one protocol ping and formats its returned Greeting as a command reply.',[
'Read the required host through Command, which trims strings and rejects missing, blank, null or wrong-type values.',
'Find the first colon. A host without one returns null immediately, before looking up Main. This differs from a status=false object.',
'Trim both pieces and parse the complete port string as a signed Java int, including supported Unicode digits. Bad syntax or overflow becomes CommandException with Invalid port. A valid int outside the socket range fails later in transport.',
'Evaluate Main.getInstance().getNIOManager(), then call the static sendPingMessage(ip, port, false). A missing Main or network fails before transport; a null NIO return does not itself prevent a static call.',
'Return response.host, response.port and response.valid. When a Greeting exists, also include its version and nullable extra data. Transport failure produces valid=false inside the otherwise successful command reply.'
],
'Native ping reuses Command, JavaStringTrim, JavaInteger, Main and the actual NIOManager transport. The no-argument Command.runCommand API now returns the existing JSONValue, which represents an object or null. All existing concrete command bodies keep building their previous JSONObject replies. Greeting.getExtraDataOptional exposes the already-stored optional JSON without dereferencing it, preserving a null extra-data value in this command. The sibling Greeting stores raw JSON text and a different default version, so it does not replace this pinned decoder.',
lambda l:'The '+l(CPP/'tools/ping_command_differential.py','ping driver')+' runs 95 programs through the actual Main/command fixtures, checking metadata, fresh prototypes, typed parameters, first-colon parsing, integer boundaries, ownership and runner behavior. Nine isolated loopback cases exercise normal, fragmented, null/nested extra data, ignored type, trailing bytes, empty/type-only frames and truncation. The shared '+l(CPP/'tools/nio_manager_transport_differential.py','transport fixture')+' independently asserts the exact SINGLE_PING plus ZERO_TXPOWID request bytes. Successful fields and failed-reply omissions are asserted separately from Java/C++ equality. The '+l(CPP/'tools/command_runner_errors_differential.py','runner error driver')+' expands to 1,680 cases, including null replies and absent/null/wrong/false status; it checks escaped exception categories and that later commands do not run. See the '+l(CPP/'student-guide/new-tests/nullable-command-replies.md','lab')+' for final build results.',
'Why does a direct ping with host:example return null, while the same command through runMultiCommand throws? Why can valid=false still appear inside a reply whose status is true?',
'These finite tests do not certify a complete node. Socket/wire diagnostic prose and enhanced Java null/cast prose are excluded; log count/order and exception categories remain compared. Full startup, every malformed Greeting branch, logger failures inside NIO and exhaustive mutable-reference behavior remain open. The counterpart is partial and parity not_verified.')
p=CPP/'student-guide/files'/relative;s=p.read_text().replace('**Port status:** `unported`; parity `not_verified`. The mapped C++ file is absent. This page does not describe a completed translation.','**Port status:** `implemented_partial`; parity `not_verified`. The mapped C++ file exists.').replace('`src/org/minima/system/commands/network/ping.cpp` (planned)','[src/org/minima/system/commands/network/ping.cpp]('+os.path.relpath(CPP/'src/org/minima/system/commands/network/ping.cpp',p.parent)+')');p.write_text(s)
for name,body in {
'src/org/minima/system/commands/Command.md':'''The no-argument runCommand API now uses the existing JSONValue because Java's JSONObject reference can be null. A concrete command still constructs its ordinary JSONObject reply, which is wrapped by the existing JSONValue constructor. String-taking helper overloads keep their object result type. This is a native representation change, not a rewrite of each command's algorithm. JSONValue can represent more kinds than Java's return type; production command bodies return objects or null, and the runner checks the object cast.''',
'src/org/minima/system/commands/CommandRunner.md':'''The runner now retains a nullable JSONValue returned by runCommand, appends it, and then reads status outside the catch block. Returning null therefore escapes as NullPointerException; returning an object with missing/null status also fails on that later access, and a non-Boolean status raises ClassCastException. No normal error reply is invented for these cases. The expanded error driver compares 1,680 requests with events and log order, including permission/parameter gates and logger failures. runSingleCommand retains an object return: a null batch result cannot reach its first-element return because the batch already failed at status access.''',
'src/org/minima/objects/Greeting.md':'''The existing optional extra-data field can contain no object after reading JSON null. The new native getExtraDataOptional accessor exposes that state for callers that forward the reference into a JSON reply. ping's loopback test sends a valid Greeting whose extra-data text is null and asserts extradata:null. Existing reference-taking getExtraData overloads remain for callers that dereference the object; their null exception categories and all mutable aliasing boundaries still need further review.''',
}.items():
 p=CPP/'student-guide/files'/name;link=os.path.relpath(CPP/'student-guide/new-tests/nullable-command-replies.md',p.parent)
 if '## Nullable replies and references' not in p.read_text():
  p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\n## Nullable replies and references\n\n'+body+' See the [nullable-reply lab]('+link+').\n')
